# Redcap Melee targets Bot2's Blazing Rootwalla, a red creature, but Ancient Adamantoise redirects the damage dealt to its
# controller's other permanents to itself (CR 614.1a). The permanent dealt the damage is the green Adamantoise, a nonred
# permanent, so Bot1 sacrifices a land (the Island); the Rootwalla is untouched and the 8/8 Adamantoise survives with 4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mountain
Redcap Melee
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Mox Ruby
Blazing Rootwalla
Forest
Forest x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot2.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot1.Choose()
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Blazing Rootwalla.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Redcap Melee.Cast(Blazing Rootwalla)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 4
Bot2.Battlefield.Blazing Rootwalla.Damage = 0
